  "description": "Patches cut from synthetic frames. Every frame is width x height, and its pixel at column i, row j has R = wave(i), G = wave(j), B = 128, where wave(n) = 5 * min(n mod 102, 102 - n mod 102). A sample point away from the frame's edge has a known value, and half a pixel off moves it by 2.5 levels. Pixel i covers [i, i + 1), so its center is at i + 0.5. Each sample names a patch pixel by row and col, the frame point (x, y) that pixel samples, and its expected rgb, black where the patch lies outside the frame. Sample points where the patch blends with the padding are left out. samples is null when the sensor's center is outside the frame, and the sensor then has no patch.",
